    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` business rule following the repo's existing conventions for derived owner fields (like `locality` and `membershipLevel`):\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` getter that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the `contactPreference` property (readOnly string) on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically from the new getter.\n\nNo controller changes were needed \u2014 the field flows through the existing `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)` mapping, so both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` return it. Both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite are green.",
